# Round XXII Track δ regression: `int a = None()` — the CALL form of the
# NoneLiteral — must REJECT at check time. Pre-fix the typechecker's Expr::Call
# arm had no special-case for `Call { callee: NoneLiteral }`; the callee typed
# as Option[?T], fell through the wildcard at `typecheck.rs:2410` and returned
# `error_id`, which unified silently against any dest type (`unify` fast-path
# at :953). Runtime observed at HEAD 0aa3f5a6 pre-fix: prints `a = 0`, both
# backends agreeing on wrong output (Core #8 both-wrong).
#
# Post-fix: the Expr::Call arm mirrors the IR lowerer at
# `src/ir/lowering/exprs/mod.rs:263` and delegates to `Expr::NoneLiteral`'s
# `decl_type_hint` logic. Here decl_type_hint = int, which is NOT Option, so
# NoneLiteral produces Option[fresh]; the surrounding unify then rejects
# Option[?T] against int cleanly (E_TypeMismatch).
#
# POSITION AXIS: var-decl. Sibling `sound_bare_none_call_in_fnarg_rejected.gg`
# covers the fn-arg position.

void main():
    int a = None()
    print(f"a = {a}")
